# USB-audio 16-channel signature walk, on out/sig8 (tests/build-sig-fixture.sh:
# track N plays a one-shot stereo tone, 200+50*(2N-1) / 200+50*(2N) Hz, so all
# sixteen USB channels carry distinct frequencies). Announce "ready" so the
# harness starts capturing, then PLAY fires the eight one-shots together and
# the tones run out gap-free for the rest of the capture. Every wait is GUEST
# time. The first gesture is 16 s after PTCH (tests/walks/trig-one.jsonl).
#
# ☠ PLAY is a PLAIN tap, not a self-verifying one. A tap carrying a lamp
# condition is redone when the condition is not met in time, and a second
# PLAY restarts the sequencer with the one-shots already fired and disarmed:
# measured as 5 s of tones then silence, and 0/16 channels loud. A lost tap
# fails the gate honestly (nothing loud); a redone one fails it misleadingly.
{"wait_text":"PTCH","timeout_ms":600000}
{"wait_guest_ms":500}
{"wait_gone":"L0ADING","timeout_ms":300000}
{"wait_guest_ms":8000}
{"mark":"ready"}
{"wait_guest_ms":8000}
{"tap":"PLAY"}
{"mark":"playing"}
{"wait_guest_ms":60000}
{"mark":"done"}
